OnePlus 15 @RELEASE_TAG@ boot-only TWRP installer
=================================================

This archive is a boot-only installer for:

  @DEVICE@
  @FIRMWARE@
  kernel release: @KERNEL_RELEASE@
  source commit: @SOURCE_COMMIT@

A release tag containing "candidate" or "test" identifies an unqualified
physical-test package. It must not be represented as stable or physically
qualified until this exact ZIP has passed the repository's device gates.

Archive contents
----------------

  boot.img
    bytes: @BOOT_BYTES@
    sha256: @BOOT_SHA256@

  kernel-info.txt
  checksums.sha256
  META-INF/com/google/android/update-binary
  META-INF/com/google/android/updater-script

It intentionally does not contain a custom system_dlkm image.

Required installed firmware contract
------------------------------------

The active slot must already use the untouched stock @FIRMWARE@
system_dlkm EROFS image:

  bytes checked: @STOCK_SYSTEM_DLKM_BYTES@
  EROFS magic at offset 1024: @STOCK_SYSTEM_DLKM_EROFS_MAGIC@
  sha256: @STOCK_SYSTEM_DLKM_SHA256@

The installer verifies the active slot, CPH2747/Canoe identity, the exact
firmware manifest, EROFS magic, and this stock system_dlkm hash before any
write. It refuses an active OTA snapshot/merge, ext4 system_dlkm, a modified
system_dlkm, an unknown firmware, or a device that cannot be verified.

What it does
------------

* Extracts and SHA-256 verifies boot.img.
* Creates a durable backup of boot_<active-slot>.
* Flashes only boot_<active-slot>.
* Reads back exactly @BOOT_BYTES@ bytes and verifies the boot SHA-256.
* Restores the boot backup if writing or read-back verification fails.

What it never does
------------------

* It never writes, mounts, maps, unmaps, resizes, erases, or otherwise changes
  system_dlkm or system_dlkm_oki.
* It never writes vendor_boot, vendor_dlkm, dtbo, vbmeta, vbmeta_system, or
  vbmeta_vendor.
* It does not modify dynamic-partition metadata or disable AVB verification.

Requirements
------------

* An unlocked OnePlus 15 on the exact firmware above.
* A TWRP build with lpdump and normal Android recovery tools.
* Decrypted /data or durable mounted external storage for the boot backup.

Install the ZIP from TWRP, then reboot System without switching slots. This is
firmware-specific: do not install it on any other OxygenOS build.

The generated system_dlkm.flatten.ext4.img remains a development and recovery
fallback artifact. It is not part of this boot-only installer.
